# CEG: bible-project-variants — variants page branch
# Branch of bible-project.ceg (root split, 2026-11-12, Kit's authoring
# lesson): single-page branch, so the page input itself is dropped —
# every state in this file is the variants page. Product documentation
# lives in bible-project.ceg's header.
# Parser note: effect descriptions are single-line in this file (the
# pre-split graph carried a multiline e19 description that ceg.py
# rejects; the full wording is preserved in this header comment):
# e19 — variants page shows the Hebrew word drop-down (empty with an
# explanatory note until academic/textual variants are loaded; v1
# data-artifact rows excluded per Kit 2026-10-01).
# Branch convention: effects whose pre-split rule was the page alone
# (e19, e37 — they hold whenever this page renders) are encoded as one
# rule per state of c11, the branch's selection input, since the
# format has no condition-less rule. Semantically identical.

[PAGE]
Bible website page (v2): variants.

[INPUTS]
c10 = variant_search : empty | text
c11 = variant_word : none | valid | invalid
c12 = variants_present : no | yes

[CONSTRAINTS]
# One page, three fields: the search text, the selected word (one and
# only one selection state), and whether that word has variants. No
# foreign-page inputs exist in this branch to constrain against.

[SUCCESS]
e19 = variants page shows the Hebrew word drop-down (empty with an explanatory note until academic/textual variants are loaded; v1 data-artifact rows excluded per Kit 2026-10-01)
e19 <= c11=none
e19 <= c11=valid
e19 <= c11=invalid
e20 = search filters the drop-down to matching Hebrew words
e20 <= c10=text
e21 = selecting a valid word with variants shows its variant readings table
e21 <= c11=valid AND c12=yes
e37 = the variants drop-down lists only words having two or more distinct variant readings after medial/final letterform folding
e37 <= c11=none
e37 <= c11=valid
e37 <= c11=invalid

[FAIL]
f7 = variants page shows "Unknown word id" for a nonexistent word id
f7 <= c11=invalid
f8 = variants page shows "No variants recorded" for a word with no variants
f8 <= c11=valid AND c12=no

[REQUIREMENTS]
REQ-BB-011 : variants page offers the Hebrew word drop-down (only words with two or more distinct variant readings) with search, shows variant readings for a selected word, and handles unknown/empty cases (index link half, e22, in bible-project.ceg) -> e19, e20, e21, e37, f7, f8
